# 📊 Complexity

## Worst case:

* Number of topo orders = **exponential (O(n!))**

So:

* ❌ Not scalable for large graphs
* ✅ Only used for small graphs / interview / theoretical problems

---

# 🔥 Key Insights (VERY important)

### 1. Kahn’s algorithm vs this

| Task             | Method           |
| ---------------- | ---------------- |
| One topo order   | BFS (Kahn)       |
| Check uniqueness | queue size check |
| All topo orders  | backtracking     |

---

### 2. Why LC 444 does NOT use this

Because:

> It only cares if the order is UNIQUE, not all possibilities

So instead of exploring all paths, it:

* Detects branching (multiple indegree-0 nodes)

---

### 3. Mental model

Think of it like:

> Each time you choose a node, you're creating a "timeline branch"

All topological orders = exploring ALL timelines.

